From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000050 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Petr Parkan Janda <petronijus@bastla.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 11:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: OMAP4: HS: configure CPU1's CP15 through the PPA on 4460 too

omap4_secondary_init() calls PPA service 0x25 (OMAP4_PPA_CPU_ACTRL_SMP_INDEX)
on secondary CPUs only for OMAP443x HS. On OMAP446x HS the same service is
what sets the Cortex-A9 Diagnostic register bits for errata 742230, 743622
and 751472 (0x850) on CPU1. A non-secure kernel cannot set them itself --
those errata options depend on !ARCH_MULTIPLATFORM for that reason -- and
the ROM sets them on CPU0 at cold boot, but CPU1's secondary boot does not.
So on a 4460 HS CPU1 has been running without the three workarounds.

Measured on a Nexus Q (4460 HS) with the SAR breadcrumbs of patch 0049,
CPU1's Diagnostic register:

  after secondary boot                0x00000000
  as the ROM hands it back from OFF   0x00000000
  after omap4_cpu_resume's PPA 0x25   0x00000850   (CPU0: 0x850 throughout)

It is also why a CPU1 OFF from cpuidle hung the board: cpu_ca9mp_do_resume()
compares the saved Diagnostic value (0) with the live one (0x850), finds them
different, and writes the secure-only register from non-secure -- an
undefined instruction taken with the MMU off.

Stock 3.0.8 issues this service on CPU1 on every wake, with CPU0 running
(ppa_cp15_cpu1_configure, 0xc0067978), which is the API's stated
precondition and holds during secondary init. Issue it for every OMAP44xx HS
secondary. The resume path retries until the service returns 0; do the same
here, bounded, and say so if it never succeeds.

Signed-off-by: Petr Parkan Janda <petronijus@bastla.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-omap2/omap-smp.c b/arch/arm/mach-omap2/omap-smp.c
index bf06c02..1ac16a4 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-omap2/omap-smp.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-omap2/omap-smp.c
@@ -152,10 +152,36 @@ static void omap4_secondary_init(unsigned int cpu)
 	 * while executing NS_SMP API on CPU1 and PPA version must be 1.4.0+.
 	 * OMAP443X GP devices- SMP bit isn't accessible.
 	 * OMAP446X GP devices - SMP bit access is enabled on both CPUs.
+	 *
+	 * The same API also configures CPU1's CP15 on OMAP446X HS, and there
+	 * it is not optional: it is what sets the Cortex-A9 Diagnostic
+	 * register bits for errata 742230, 743622 and 751472 (0x850), which a
+	 * non-secure kernel cannot set itself (those errata options depend on
+	 * !ARCH_MULTIPLATFORM). The ROM sets them on CPU0 at cold boot; CPU1's
+	 * secondary boot does not, so without this call CPU1 runs with
+	 * Diagnostic == 0. Measured on a 4460 HS (Nexus Q): CPU1 0x000 after
+	 * boot, 0x850 only after omap4_cpu_resume's ppa_actrl_retry. Besides
+	 * the missing workarounds, cpu_ca9mp_do_resume() then finds the saved
+	 * 0 differing from the live 0x850 on the first CPU OFF, writes the
+	 * secure-only register from non-secure and hangs with the MMU off.
+	 * Stock 3.0.8 issued this call on CPU1 on every wake
+	 * (ppa_cp15_cpu1_configure), with CPU0 running as here.
+	 *
+	 * The resume path retries until the API returns 0; do the same here,
+	 * bounded, since a secondary that cannot configure itself should say so.
 	 */
-	if (soc_is_omap443x() && (omap_type() != OMAP2_DEVICE_TYPE_GP))
-		omap_secure_dispatcher(OMAP4_PPA_CPU_ACTRL_SMP_INDEX,
-							4, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0);
+	if (soc_is_omap44xx() && (omap_type() != OMAP2_DEVICE_TYPE_GP)) {
+		int tries = 10;
+		u32 ret;
+
+		do {
+			ret = omap_secure_dispatcher(OMAP4_PPA_CPU_ACTRL_SMP_INDEX,
+						     4, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0);
+		} while (ret && --tries);
+		if (ret)
+			pr_warn("CPU%u: PPA CP15/ACTRL configure failed: %u\n",
+				cpu, ret);
+	}
 
 	if (soc_is_omap54xx() || soc_is_dra7xx()) {
 		/*
